# AION × Superpowers bridge

This factory uses [obra/superpowers](https://github.com/obra/superpowers) as **session process**, layered under AION governance.

## Priority (highest first)

1. Explicit human/CEO instruction for this turn
2. `AION_ENGINEERING.md`, active `missions/*`, `AGENTS.md`
3. `docs/workflows/*`, `docs/templates/*`, `docs/standards/*`
4. Superpowers skills (if the plugin is installed)
5. Default agent behavior

## Before creative or implementation work

1. Confirm active mission scope and acceptance criteria.
2. Prefer Superpowers `brainstorming` for new behavior; write outcomes into AION artifacts (mission/PRD/architecture/task), not only chat.
3. Prefer `writing-plans` / Architect tasks before large code changes.
4. Prefer `test-driven-development` for logic changes; match depth to `docs/standards/TESTING.md`.
5. Prefer `verification-before-completion` before any "done / fixed / passing" claim.
6. Prefer `systematic-debugging` before speculative bugfixes.

## Hard stops Superpowers must not override

- CEO approval gates (mission scope, production deploy, release, validation close)
- Security review triggers in `docs/workflows/END_TO_END.md`
- Secrets in git/logs/prompts
- Out-of-scope mission items
- Implementing product features in this factory repo (product code lives in product repos)

## Role shortcuts

| Role | Lean on |
|------|---------|
| PM | brainstorming → Mission + PRD templates |
| Architect | brainstorming → writing-plans → ARCHITECTURE + TASK templates |
| Builder | worktrees → executing-plans/TDD → PR |
| QA | verification-before-completion → QA_REPORT |
| Security | template review; systematic-debugging for investigations |
| Release | verification + release record; never silent prod ship |

